The [[Psi Harmonizer]] Q target (> 500) exceeds what the standard composite formulation can deliver. This is an unsolved engineering problem — the [[Psi Harmonizer]] will require either a lower-loss fill (perhaps replacing MWCNT with vapour-grown carbon fibres at lower loading) or a cavity geometry that reduces the effective filling factor of the lossy phases.

The [[ψ Memory Element]] Q requirement (> 10⁶) is not achievable with any room-temperature composite. This page records the target as an engineering specification — the physics requires it — while noting that the material science solution is a future research problem.

== Ringdown Time and Anchor Burst Duration ==

The ringdown time <math>\tau</math> (e-folding time of amplitude after drive cut) and Anchor burst duration <math>t_{\rm burst}</math> must satisfy:

:<math>\tau = \frac{2Q_\psi}{\omega_0}, \qquad t_{\rm burst} \gg \tau_{\rm establish}</math>

where <math>\tau_{\rm establish}</math> is the time required for the ψ field to build up from zero to its steady-state amplitude when the drive is first applied — approximately <math>2Q_\psi/\omega_0</math> (the same as the ringdown time, by time-reversal symmetry).

At the [[Psi Stabilizer]] design point:

:<math>\tau = \frac{2 \times 200}{2\pi \times 4\times10^4} \approx 1.6\,\text{ms}</math>

The 90-second Anchor burst is 56,000 times longer than the field establishment time. The Anchor drive is entirely dominated by steady-state operation — the establishment transient is negligible. This is not universally true:

{| class="wikitable" style="width:100%;"
! Module !! <math>Q_\psi</math> !! Frequency (kHz) !! <math>\tau</math> (ms) !! Anchor burst duration !! <math>t_{\rm burst}/\tau</math>
|-
| [[Psi Stabilizer]] || 200 || 40 || 1.6 || 90 s || 56,250 — establishment negligible
|-
| [[Psi Harmonizer]] || 500 || 10 || 16 || 90 s || 5,625 — still negligible
|-
| [[ψ Memory Element]] || 10⁶ || 100,000 || 3,180 (3.18 s) || Written in 100 ms pulses || 0.031 — establishment dominates! Must account for in write protocol
|}

The [[ψ Memory Element]] write protocol must explicitly account for the field establishment transient — a 100 ms write pulse at Q = 10⁶ reaches only 3% of steady-state amplitude. The write pulse must be extended to at least <math>5\tau \approx 16</math> s for the field to reach 99% of its target amplitude.

